TensorFold: the MIT notice that survives from before v0.6.0
==========================================================

This image installs [TensorFold](https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold) and applies the
vendored recipe's patches to the installed package, so TensorFold's code — patched — ships
inside the image. TensorFold moved to the Apache License 2.0 at v0.6.0; code written before
v0.6.0 keeps its MIT notice, which this file retains for that portion of the engine.

The notice below is reproduced verbatim from the upstream recipe's `NOTICE` file
(`MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold` at commit
`05397e24ee1fa0a60df11ff5dcb7a68f45cff6cd`), which is vendored unmodified as
`recipe/NOTICE`. TensorFold's own `NOTICE` reads: "TensorFold / Copyright 2026 TensorFold
contributors / https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold".

Note on the upstream license: the upstream recipe is **Apache-2.0**, not AGPL-3.0 and not
MIT. The only MIT material it carries is TensorFold's pre-v0.6.0 notice below (and
ExLlamaV3, credited for the EXL3 format but not bundled in this image). See
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

